27se|n|A solemn promise made to God, or to some deity; an act by which one consecrates or devotes himself, absolutely or conditionally, wholly or in part, for a longer or shorter time, to some act, service, or condition; a devotion of one's possessions; as, a baptismal vow; a vow of poverty. ; Specifically, a promise of fidelity; a pledge of love or affection; as, the marriage vow. ; To give, consecrate, or dedicate to God, or to some deity, by a solemn promise; to devote; to promise solemnly. ; To assert solemnly; to asseverate.	v:7qj,93,3~7qj,93,3	n:7qj,88,2~7qj,88,2
